    "description": "What if multiple internet connections could work together to download one file?\n\nMeet Plexo, an open-source download manager that splits files into chunks and downloads them in parallel across independent connections.\n\nFor example, it can use your Wi-Fi and a USB-tethered phone connection at the same time to potentially boost download speeds.\n\nFollow @ai4today for more tech, breakthroughs, and innovation driving the AI revolution.\n\n🔗 GitHub: \nhttps://github.com/anmolkapil/plexo\n\n#AI #OpenSource #Internet #DownloadManager #Innovation",
